# Known findings of tests/qc/act_keep.js. Each line is one pattern (a JavaScript regular expression) matched against a FAIL line.
# A listed failure does not fail the run. A listed line that no longer matches any failure DOES fail the run, so take it out when the app is fixed.
# Empty on purpose: the main session decides which findings in LANE_act_keep.md are fixed and which are named here.
# Example:  ^FAIL setName: REPLACES
# MAIN 3, 2026-11-19 (the coordinator's rule for v1): an action that sets ONE typed value keeps no 3-day copy. Its Undo lasts for the visit and must be exact
# (the pattern below only matches while it is). Reason: there is one copy slot, and a small edit must not push out the copy of a big change.
# Bulk and removing actions (tx from the assistant or setup from statements, removeGoal, removeLine, removeReceipts, removeCard, sweep, unsweep, release) are NOT listed: they keep the copy.
^FAIL (setPay|setIncome|setBalance|setBankNow|setCard|setMinBalance|setCeiling|setLine|renameLine|setLineEnds|updateGoal|setGoalSaving|setAims|setName|setCurrency|setHome): (REPLACES|REMOVES) .*NO COPY in the saved data; Undo now is exact
# Undo itself has no redo. Named until Mako asks for one.
^FAIL undo: REPLACES
# MAIN 7, 2026-11-19: drawNow (7424a46, F4) only repaints the page that was held back while a burrow is open. It changes no saved data, so there is no copy to keep and no call that would show an effect.
^FAIL drawNow: UNKNOWN
